# Designer Profile

## Overview

You are working on a modular synthesizer UI built with Svelte 5 and Tailwind CSS. The UI package lives in `packages/ui` and the web app in `apps/web`.

## Technology Stack

- **Svelte 5** - Using runes API (`$props`, `$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`)
- **Tailwind CSS** - Utility-first styling with custom design tokens
- **Storybook** - Component development and documentation
- **tailwind-merge** - For conditional class merging

## Component Architecture

### Directory Structure
```
packages/ui/src/
├── components/       # Reusable UI primitives
│   ├── Button.svelte
│   ├── Input.svelte
│   ├── Knob/         # Complex components in folders
│   ├── Switch.svelte
│   └── ...
├── modules/          # Synth module UIs
│   ├── Oscillator/
│   ├── Filter.svelte
│   ├── shared/       # Panel, Plug components
│   └── ...
├── actions/          # Svelte actions (drag, wheel)
├── range/            # Value range/scaling utilities
└── types/            # TypeScript types
```

### Svelte 5 Runes Patterns

#### Props with Runes
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  interface MyComponentProps {
    value: number
    disabled?: boolean
    onChange?: (value: number) => void
  }

  let {
    value,
    disabled = false,
    onChange
  }: MyComponentProps = $props()
</script>
```

#### Derived State
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  let count = $state(0)
  let doubled = $derived(count * 2)
</script>
```

#### Effects with Cleanup
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  $effect(() => {
    const handler = () => { /* ... */ }
    element.addEventListener('click', handler)
    return () => element.removeEventListener('click', handler)
  })
</script>
```

#### Snippets (Replaces Slots)
```svelte
<!-- Parent -->
<Panel>
  {#snippet children()}
    <div>Content here</div>
  {/snippet}
  {#snippet outputs()}
    <Plug ctx={routing.output} />
  {/snippet}
</Panel>

<!-- Panel.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  let { children, outputs }: { children: Snippet, outputs?: Snippet } = $props()
</script>

<div class="panel">
  {@render children()}
  <div class="outputs">
    {#if outputs}
      {@render outputs()}
    {/if}
  </div>
</div>
```

## Design System

### CSS Custom Properties
Module colors use CSS variables for theming:
```css
--color-module-accent    /* Border and accent color */
--color-module-background /* Panel background */
--color-light            /* Light text/icons */
--color-dark             /* Dark text/icons */
```

Each module defines its own color scheme:
```svelte
<Panel
  --color-module-accent="var(--color-pink)"
  --color-module-background="var(--color-pink-dark)"
>
```

### Grid System
- Base unit: `0.5rem` (8px)
- Modules positioned on grid: `grid-column`, `grid-row`
- Module dimensions in grid units: `width={8}` = 8 grid cells wide

### Typography
- Font: Mono for values/labels, system for UI
- Sizes: `text-xs` for labels, standard for controls

## Module UI Pattern

Every synth module follows this structure:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import Panel from '../shared/Panel.svelte'
  import Plug from '../shared/Plug.svelte'
  import Knob from '../../components/Knob/Knob.svelte'
  import type { BaseModuleProps } from '../../types/props'

  interface ModuleProps extends BaseModuleProps {
    node: ModuleNode
  }

  let {
    node,
    disabled = false,
    position,
    onClose,
    onClone,
    onDrag,
    onPlugClick,
    bindPlugElement,
    bindElement
  }: ModuleProps = $props()

  const state = intoReadable(node.state)
  const routing = node.getRoutingDefinition()
</script>

<Panel
  name={node.name}
  {position}
  {disabled}
  {onClose}
  {onClone}
  {onDrag}
  {bindElement}
  height={8}
  width={8}
  --color-module-accent="var(--color-blue)"
  --color-module-background="var(--color-blue-dark)"
>
  {#snippet children()}
    <!-- Controls: Knobs, Switches, etc. -->
    <Knob bind:value={$state.frequency} range={frequencyRange} label="freq">
      <div slot="knob-inputs">
        <Plug ctx={routing.frequency} onClick={onPlugClick} bindElement={bindPlugElement} />
      </div>
    </Knob>
  {/snippet}

  {#snippet outputs()}
    <Plug ctx={routing.output} onClick={onPlugClick} bindElement={bindPlugElement} />
  {/snippet}
</Panel>
```

## Interactive Controls

### Knob Component
- Drag vertically to change value
- Shift+drag for fine control (0.1x speed)
- Double-click to type value
- Mouse wheel support
- Supports CV input plugs

### Range System
Ranges define how values are scaled and displayed:

```typescript
import { RangeType, Scale, type ContinuousRange } from '../range/range'

const frequencyRange: ContinuousRange = {
  type: RangeType.Continuous,
  start: 20,
  end: 20000,
  scale: { type: Scale.Logarithmic },
  valueToString: (v) => `${v.toFixed(0)} Hz`,
  stringToValue: (v, unit) => v // Parse from string
}

const choiceRange: ChoiceRange = {
  type: RangeType.Choice,
  choices: [
    { label: 'Sine', value: 0 },
    { label: 'Square', value: 1 }
  ]
}
```

### Custom Actions
Located in `packages/ui/src/actions/`:

```svelte
<div
  use:useDrag={{ onDrag: handleDrag, onDragStart: captureStart }}
  use:useWheel={{ onWheel: handleWheel }}
>
```

## Storybook

Every component should have stories for documentation:

```typescript
// Component.stories.ts
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/svelte'
import Component from './Component.svelte'

const meta: Meta<Component> = {
  title: 'Modules/Component',
  component: Component,
  tags: ['autodocs']
}

export default meta
type Story = StoryObj<typeof meta>

export const Default: Story = {
  args: {
    value: 0.5,
    disabled: false
  }
}
```

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML (`button`, `input`, not `div`)
- Add `role="slider"` for custom controls
- Include `aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax`
- Ensure keyboard navigation (`tabindex="0"`)
- Support for disabled state styling

## Performance

- Use `$derived` instead of reactive statements where possible
- Avoid expensive computations in render
- Use CSS transforms for animations (GPU accelerated)
- Minimize DOM updates during drag operations
